ype\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Could have/couldn't have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"past ability, how you had this option in the past but now the choice no longer exists.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">You <span class=\\\"strong\\\">could have been </span>famous- you were really good at playing tennis.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Should have/shouldn't have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"past obligation, something that you had to do in the past for the result to be favourable now\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">shouldn't have said</span> that to Mrs. Black, I wasn't thinking about it.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Would have/wouldn't have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" past conditional construction, a condition that existed in the past but does not anymore\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">We <span class=\\\"strong\\\">wouldn't have gone </span> to the party if we had known they would be there.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"May have/may not have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"past possibility, they usually describe something about which you are not quite certain.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">may have left</span> it at home, but I'm not sure.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Must have/must not have \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"past probability, something of which you are nearly certain but of which you are not quite sure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">He <span class=\\\"strong\\\">must not have heard </span>me properly because I didn't say that.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "She must have had some inclination. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I told her she should have told me earlier. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I could have been part of the decision process."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I wouldn't have done that."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I may have just blew it again!"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Comparative Clause: As ...  As"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can show comparisons and contrast using the structure as ... as ..."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use as ... as in the following pattern:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "(not) <span class=\"strong\">as </span>adjective/adverb <span class=\"strong\">as</span></br>   <span class=\"italic\">She is not<span class=\"strong\"> as independent as </span>her sister.</br> An only child develops <span class=\"strong\">as well as </span>a child with siblings."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use as ... as in these ways: <ol><li> to emphasize two equal elements<br/>Example:</br><span class=\"italic\">He is as strong as his brother.</span></li> <li>  to show that two things are slightly unequal</br>Example:</br><span class = \"italic\">Jim does not like comedies as much as I do.</span> </li> <li> to emphasize a difference</br>Example:</br><span class = \"italic\">She is not as artistic as I am.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'm not as independent as Amy. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "As smart and adventurous as me? "}, {"type": "example", "content": "She is as tall as you are too."}, {"type": "example", "content": "She can't dance as well as you can. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I know she cares about our relationship as much as I do."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to blow it"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to make a big mistake"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I may have just blew it again."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le16ob06aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use if you think you made a big mistake."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "inclination"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " a person's natural tendency to act or feel a particular way"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She must have had some inclination."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le16ob06aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to dump"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to end a romantic relationship"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I'm scared that she is going to dump me."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le16ob06aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to construe"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to interpret words or actions in a particular way"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Did you say anything really terrible that could be construed as a deal breaker?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le16ob06aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "captivating"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "capable of attracting and holding interest"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I hear it's a captivating place."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le16ob06aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "spectacular"}, {"type": "definition", 